1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:11,580
Some of us like to keep some things private – maybe we don’t want people knowing about our relationship status, our age or where we live – because these details are personal.
我们中有些人总喜欢保留一些隐私——可能不愿让别人知道自己的感情状况、年龄或是住址，因为这些都属于个人私密信息。

2
00:00:11,580 --> 00:00:18,840
The problem is, everywhere we go online, we seem to leave a digital footprint.
但问题在于，我们在网络上的每一次足迹，似乎都会留下数字痕迹。

3
00:00:18,840 --> 00:00:26,810
On our social media accounts, we often display things like our opinions, connections and holiday snaps.
我们常常会在社交媒体账号上分享自己的观点、社交关系和度假照片。

4
00:00:26,810 --> 00:00:31,820
The issue is, how do we stop everybody seeing everything?
但问题是，如何才能避免自己的所有信息被所有人看到呢？

5
00:00:31,820 --> 00:00:36,100
Maybe we don’t want a random stranger knowing our favourite type of coffee.
或许我们并不想让陌生路人知道自己爱喝哪种咖啡。

6
00:00:36,100 --> 00:00:43,360
And cookies – there was a time they were just something nice to eat. Now they seem to be popping up on websites.
还有“Cookie”——曾几何时，这个词还只指代美味的甜点，如今却频频出现在各类网站中。

7
00:00:43,360 --> 00:00:46,520
So how can you stay more private?
那么，怎样才能更好地保护自己的网络隐私呢？

8
00:00:46,520 --> 00:00:49,290
There are some steps you can take.
其实我们可以采取一些措施。

9
00:00:49,290 --> 00:00:54,030
First, on your social media accounts, check your privacy settings.
首先，查看自己社交媒体账号的隐私设置。

10
00:00:54,030 --> 00:01:02,230
Many social media platforms allow everything to be visible by default, and the onus is on you to set your boundaries.
许多社交平台默认将所有内容设为公开可见，因此设置信息分享边界的责任需要由你自己承担。

11
00:01:02,230 --> 00:01:07,040
And limiting the amount you share isn’t only confined to social media.
而且限制分享内容这件事，并不仅限于社交媒体。

12
00:01:07,040 --> 00:01:17,940
There are many sites out there that help you to share documents – so a good tip may be to not put anything too private, like passwords, on there.
有很多网站都提供文件分享功能，一个实用的小建议是，不要在这些平台上传过于私密的内容，比如密码之类的信息。

13
00:01:17,940 --> 00:01:21,190
One errant click may send it to the wrong person.
一个误操作的点击，就可能把信息发给错误的对象。

14
00:01:21,190 --> 00:01:32,810
Finally, cookies are designed to improve your browsing experience by tracking and saving information about your visits to a site, helping to personalise your sessions.
最后需要说明的是，网站Cookie的设计初衷，是通过追踪并保存用户的网站访问记录，来优化浏览体验，实现个性化的访问服务。

15
00:01:32,810 --> 00:01:40,760
Deleting your browsing history may help, but there are certain apps which can block them if you don’t feel comfortable.
删除浏览记录或许能起到一定作用，但如果你对此仍有顾虑，也可以借助一些专门的应用程序来拦截Cookie。

16
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:55,100
So, if you want to maintain your privacy online, maybe only share things you’d be happy with a stranger seeing – and if you don’t feel comfortable with cookies, you might decide to invest in some tech to block them.
所以，如果你想保护自己的网络隐私，不妨只分享那些即便是陌生人看到也无妨的内容。而如果对网站Cookie心存芥蒂，你可以考虑借助相关技术工具来拦截它们。

17
00:01:55,100 --> 00:02:02,660
If that’s not enough, just don’t accept them and visit another site – and why not have a yummy cookie to eat instead?
要是这些方法还不够，那就直接拒绝Cookie，换一个网站访问吧——与此同时，何不享用一块美味的曲奇饼干呢？
